.TH PILA 1 "" "Pila" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pila \- a stacking Wayland compositor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pila
.RB [ \-c | \-\-command
.IR CMD ]
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-backend
.BR winit | udev | headless ]
.RB [ \-\-headless\-outputs
.IR OUTPUTS ]
.br
.B pila \-\-check\-config
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR FILE ]
.br
.B pila msg
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.I request
.br
.B pila\-session
.br
.B pila\-report
.RI [ file ]
.br
.B pila\-check
.RB [ \-\-nested ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pila
is a stacking Wayland compositor featuring overlapping windows with title bars, edge and corner
snapping, workspaces spanning all monitors, configurable animations, and per-app rules.
Configuration lives in a single TOML file that reloads automatically on save.
X11 apps run via Xwayland, started on demand when the first X11 client connects (and optionally
stopped when idle via
.BR "[xwayland] idle-timeout" );
set
.B "[xwayland] enabled = false"
to disable X11 support entirely.
The default
.B autostart
runs
.BR swayidle ,
which locks the screen with
.B swaylock
after 5 minutes of inactivity and before sleep, and powers off monitors after 10 minutes (any
input wakes them).
.PP
Started from a display manager or TTY, Pila drives monitors and input devices directly.
Started inside another desktop session, it opens nested in a window with Alt as the Mod key.
.PP
.B pila\-session
launches Pila as a login session, logging to
.I ~/.local/state/pila/pila.log
and starting a D\-Bus session bus via
.B dbus\-run\-session
if one is not already present.
Display managers invoke it automatically; from a TTY, run it after logging in.
.PP
.B pila\-report
collects diagnostic info for bug reports (version, OS, GPU, monitors, config validation, and recent
log lines) into
.I file
(default:
.IR pila\-report.txt ),
redacting your username, hostname, and home directory.
Nothing is uploaded automatically.
.PP
.B pila\-check
benchmarks and smoke-tests Pila on your hardware.
Run from a spare TTY while no graphical session is active, it drives real programs for roughly a
minute (windows, workspaces, screen capture, blur, fullscreen), prints PASS or FAIL per check along
with frame times and monitor latency, and writes its log to
.IR ~/.local/state/pila/pila\-tty.log .
Pass
.B \-\-nested
to run inside a window on your current desktop, or
.B \-\-help
for all options.
.PP
See the user manual
.I MANUAL.md
(installed in
.I /usr/share/doc/pila
by distro packages, and online at https://github.com/igalmarino/pila) for detailed usage and
configuration.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-command " " \fICMD\fR
Run shell command
.I CMD
at startup instead of the configured
.B autostart
list (which defaults to swaybg, waybar, mako, and swayidle).
.TP
.BR \-\-config " " \fIFILE\fR
Load configuration from
.I FILE
instead of the default path (see
.BR FILES ).
.TP
.BR \-\-backend " " \fIBACKEND\fR
Select the rendering and input backend:
.B winit
opens Pila nested inside another Wayland or X11 desktop;
.B udev
drives displays and input devices directly from a TTY;
.B headless
creates virtual outputs and a control socket
(\fI$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR\fP/\fIWAYLAND_DISPLAY\fP.control)
for automated testing.
Defaults to
.B winit
when
.B WAYLAND_DISPLAY
or
.B DISPLAY
is set, and
.B udev
otherwise.
.TP
.BR \-\-headless\-outputs " " \fIOUTPUTS\fR
Comma-separated virtual output definitions for the headless backend:
.IR NAME : W x H [@ HZ ][= MAKE / MODEL [/ SERIAL ]]
(default: HEADLESS\-1:1280x800@60).
.TP
.B \-\-check\-config
Validate the configuration file and XKB keymap, report any errors or warnings, and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage summary and exit.
.SH PILA MSG
.B pila msg
communicates with a running Pila instance:
.TP
.BR "pila msg " [ \-\-json ] " windows" | outputs | workspaces | keyboard | colors | switch | focused | version
Query windows, enabled monitors, workspaces, keyboard layouts,
.B [colors]
values, active window-switcher state, the focused window, or Pila's version.
.TP
.BR "pila msg " [ \-\-json ] " subscribe " [ windows | workspaces | outputs | keyboard | colors | switch ...]
Stream full state snapshots whenever any subscribed category changes, until Pila exits.
.TP
.BI "pila msg action " action
Execute a bindable action (for example,
.BR "workspace 2" ).
.TP
.BI "pila msg focus " id ", pila msg close " id ", pila msg minimize " id
Focus, close, or minimize a window by the
.I id
returned by
.B pila msg windows
(focusing a minimized window restores it).
.TP
.BR "pila msg " [ \-\-json ] " screen\-shares"
List the screen shares remembered for apps, which they get again without the share picker.
.TP
.BI "pila msg forget\-screen\-share " id\fR|\fBall
Forget a remembered screen share by the
.I id
returned by
.BR "pila msg screen\-shares" ,
or all of them.
.TP
.BR "pila msg " [ \-\-json ] " capture\-permissions"
List the programs allowed in the prompt to capture the screen directly (wlr-screencopy,
ext-image-copy-capture) when
.B [permissions] enforce
is on, until you log out; rules in the configuration aren't listed.
.TP
.BI "pila msg forget\-capture\-permission " id\fR|\fBall
Forget a capture permission by the
.I id
returned by
.BR "pila msg capture\-permissions" ,
or all of them; the program's captures stop.
.TP
.BR "pila msg " [ \-\-json ] " captures"
List the programs capturing the screen now (through the portal, ext-image-copy-capture or
wlr-screencopy) and what each captures, then the capture that ended last and how long ago; with
.BR \-\-waybar ,
follow them as a waybar custom module.
.TP
.BR "pila msg " [ \-\-json ] " idle\-inhibitors"
List the apps keeping the screen on now: those that asked over D-Bus
.RB ( org.freedesktop.ScreenSaver )
and the visible windows and layer surfaces with a Wayland idle inhibitor.
.PP
Scripts should pass
.BR \-\-json ,
as plain-text output is formatted for humans and may change.
Run
.B pila msg \-\-help
for full syntax.
Exit codes: 0 on success, 1 if Pila refused the request, 2 for invalid arguments, 3 if Pila could
not be reached.
.SH DEFAULT BINDINGS
Mod defaults to Super on a TTY or login session and Alt when nested, unless overridden with
.B mod
in the configuration.
Setting
.B default-bindings = false
disables all default bindings and gestures so only your own apply.
.TP
.B Mod+Return
Open a terminal.
.TP
.B Mod+D
Open the configured launcher (default:
.BR fuzzel ;
does nothing if not installed).
.TP
.B Mod
Tap and release alone (with no other key, click, scroll, or gesture) to open the launcher.
.TP
.BR Mod+Tab ", " Mod+J
Switch to the previously focused window; hold Mod and tap again to cycle further back.
.TP
.B Mod+Shift+Tab
Cycle through windows in reverse order.
.TP
.BR Alt+Tab ", " Alt+Shift+Tab
Same as Mod+Tab and Mod+Shift+Tab regardless of the Mod setting.
.TP
.B Mod+W
Toggle the overview, spreading workspace windows out without overlap below a live workspace strip.
Select with clicks or arrow keys and Enter; click a workspace to switch or drag a window onto it to
move it; Escape closes.
.TP
.B Mod+M
Toggle maximize.
.TP
.B Mod+N
Minimize the focused window.
.TP
.B Mod+F
Toggle fullscreen.
.TP
.BR Mod+Left ", " Mod+Right
Snap to the left or right half (or shift a quarter-snapped window to the adjacent quarter); press
again toward the same edge to restore.
.TP
.B Mod+Up
Maximize a floating window or top quarter; snap a half to its top quarter; expand a bottom quarter
back to a half.
.TP
.B Mod+Down
Restore a maximized window or bottom quarter; snap a half to its bottom quarter; expand a top
quarter back to a half.
.TP
.BR Mod+Shift+Left ", " Mod+Shift+Right ", " Mod+Shift+Up ", " Mod+Shift+Down
Move the focused window.
.TP
.BR Mod+Ctrl+Right ", " Mod+Ctrl+Down ", " Mod+Ctrl+Left ", " Mod+Ctrl+Up
Grow or shrink window width and height.
.TP
.B Mod+C
Center the focused window.
.TP
.B Mod+T
Toggle always-on-top.
.TP
.B Mod+P
Toggle visible on all workspaces.
.TP
.B Mod+H
Minimize all windows on the current workspace (show desktop); press again to restore.
.TP
.BR Mod+O ", " Mod+Shift+O
Focus the next monitor; move the focused window to the next monitor.
.TP
.BR Mod+1 " .. " Mod+9 ", " Mod+Shift+1 " .. " Mod+Shift+9
Switch to a workspace; move the focused window to a workspace.
.TP
.BR Mod+Page_Down ", " Mod+Page_Up
Switch to the next or previous workspace.
.TP
.BR Mod+Shift+Page_Down ", " Mod+Shift+Page_Up
Move the focused window to the next or previous workspace.
.TP
.BR Mod+WheelScrollDown ", " Mod+WheelScrollUp
Switch to the next or previous workspace with the mouse wheel (cooldown set by
.BR wheel-binding-cooldown ).
.TP
.BR Mod+Shift+WheelScrollDown ", " Mod+Shift+WheelScrollUp
Move the focused window to the next or previous workspace.
.TP
.B Mod+Shift+S
Capture a selected region to the clipboard (grim, slurp, wl-copy).
.TP
.B Mod+Ctrl+S
Save a screenshot of the monitor under the pointer to ~/Pictures (grim).
.TP
.BR XF86AudioRaiseVolume ", " XF86AudioLowerVolume
Adjust volume up or down by 5% (wpctl).
.TP
.BR XF86AudioMute ", " XF86AudioMicMute
Toggle speaker or microphone mute (wpctl).
.TP
.BR XF86MonBrightnessUp ", " XF86MonBrightnessDown
Adjust screen brightness up or down by 5% (brightnessctl).
.TP
.BR XF86AudioPlay ", " XF86AudioPause ", " XF86AudioNext ", " XF86AudioPrev ", " XF86AudioStop
Control media playback in the active player (playerctl).
.TP
.B Mod+Shift+Q
Close the focused window.
.TP
.B Mod+Shift+E
Quit Pila, after asking: Enter, Mod+Shift+E again or Quit quits; Escape or Cancel stays
(\fBconfirm-quit\fR; the \fBquit\fR action doesn't ask).
.TP
.B Mod+Shift+slash
Toggle the shortcuts cheatsheet (Mod+?); a shorter welcome overlay appears on first run.
Any key or click dismisses it.
.TP
.BR "Mod + left drag" ", " "Mod + right drag"
Move a window; resize from its nearest corner.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Alt+F1 .. F12
Switch to another virtual terminal.
.PP
Default touchpad swipes:
.B swipe\-3\-left
and
.B swipe\-3\-right
switch windows;
.B swipe\-3\-up
toggles maximize;
.B swipe\-3\-down
restores a snapped or maximized window;
.B swipe\-4\-left
and
.B swipe\-4\-right
switch to the next and previous workspace;
.B swipe\-4\-up
and
.B swipe\-4\-down
open and close the overview.
.PP
All bindings and gestures except mouse drags (which follow
.BR mod )
and VT switching can be customized under
.B [bindings]
and
.BR [gestures] .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PILA_MOD
Override the Mod key
.RB ( super ,
.BR alt ,
or
.BR ctrl ),
taking precedence over
.BR mod .
.TP
.B PILA_TERMINAL
Override the terminal command for Mod+Return, taking precedence over
.BR terminal .
.TP
.B PILA_LAUNCHER
Override the launcher command for Mod+D and tapping Mod, taking precedence over
.BR launcher .
.TP
.BR XCURSOR_THEME ", " XCURSOR_SIZE
Fallback cursor theme and size when not set in
.B [cursor]
(defaults: default, 24; in nested mode, applies only to the shake-magnified cursor).
When configured in
.BR [cursor] ,
Pila also exports these values to launched apps.
.TP
.BR XKB_DEFAULT_LAYOUT ", " XKB_DEFAULT_VARIANT ", " XKB_DEFAULT_OPTIONS
Fallback XKB keyboard layout settings when
.B [keyboard]
leaves them unset.
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Log verbosity filter (default: info; use debug for detailed diagnostics).
.PP
Programs launched by Pila receive
.BR WAYLAND_DISPLAY ,
Xwayland's
.B DISPLAY
and
.BR XAUTHORITY ,
.BR XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP =pila,
.BR XDG_SESSION_TYPE =wayland,
and
.B PILA_SOCKET
(for
.BR "pila msg" ),
with foreign compositor variables
.RB ( SWAYSOCK ", " HYPRLAND_INSTANCE_SIGNATURE ", ...)"
stripped so desktop shells target Pila.
Commands run from keybindings also receive
.BR PILA_OUTPUT ,
naming the monitor under the pointer.
.PP
On a TTY, Pila exports
.BR WAYLAND_DISPLAY ", " DISPLAY ", " XAUTHORITY ", " XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP ", " XDG_SESSION_TYPE ,
and
.B PILA_SOCKET
to the D\-Bus session bus (and
.B "systemd \-\-user"
when running) so portals and user services inherit them.
.SH FILES
.TP
.IR ~/.config/pila/config.toml " (or " $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/pila/config.toml )
User configuration file.
Every option is documented in
.IR config.example.toml ,
installed in
.I /usr/share/doc/pila
and embedded in Pila as its default fallback.
On first start without a config file (and without
.BR \-\-config ),
Pila writes the example file there.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/pila\-tools/
Auto-generated configs for default tools (waybar, fuzzel, mako, swaylock, and swaybg's wallpaper),
passed via CLI flags when you have no config of your own, leaving
.I ~/.config
untouched.
Copy a file into
.I ~/.config
to customize it, or disable with
.BR "tool\-configs = false" .
.TP
.IR ~/.local/state/pila/pila.log " (or " $XDG_STATE_HOME/pila/pila.log )
Log file for sessions started with
.BR pila\-session ;
.I pila.log.old
holds the previous run.
Under systemd, logs are also sent to
.BR "journalctl \-t pila \-b" .
Crashes log a "pila crashed" entry with a backtrace.
.TP
.IR ~/.local/state/pila/sessions.json " (or " $XDG_STATE_HOME/pila/sessions.json )
Saved window positions and states for apps using xdg\-session\-management.
Nested and secondary instances keep this state in memory only.
.TP
.IR ~/.local/state/pila/app\-shortcuts.json " (or " $XDG_STATE_HOME/pila/app\-shortcuts.json )
Persisted global shortcut assignments confirmed through the GlobalShortcuts portal.
.TP
.IR ~/.local/state/pila/screen\-shares.json " (or " $XDG_STATE_HOME/pila/screen\-shares.json )
Screen shares remembered for apps through the ScreenCast portal's Remember toggle (listed by
.BR "pila msg screen\-shares" ).
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/pila\-screenshots/
Temporary storage for portal screenshots (last 10 kept until logout).
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/pila\-WAYLAND_DISPLAY.sock
Unix IPC socket used by
.B pila msg
(exposed to child processes as
.BR PILA_SOCKET ).
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/user/pila.service
.TQ
.I /usr/lib/systemd/user/pila\-shutdown.target
Systemd user units started by
.B pila\-session
and bound to
.BR graphical\-session.target ,
launching user services and XDG autostart entries once Pila is ready and stopping them on exit.
Set
.B PILA_NO_SYSTEMD=1
to bypass systemd and start Pila directly.
.TP
.I /etc/xdg/xdg\-desktop\-portal/pila\-portals.conf
.TQ
.I /usr/share/xdg\-desktop\-portal/portals/pila.portal
Portal configuration routing ScreenCast, Screenshot, and GlobalShortcuts to Pila and other portals
to xdg\-desktop\-portal\-gtk.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B pila
exits with 2 for invalid arguments and non-zero if startup fails.
.B pila \-\-check\-config
exits with 0 if valid and 1 if invalid.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR Xwayland (1),
.BR xkeyboard\-config (7)
.PP
https://github.com/igalmarino/pila
